## Code Example
```
// Recursion: O(2^n)
function fib(n) {
  if (n <= 1) return n;
  return fib(n-1) + fib(n-2);
}

// DP: O(n)
function fibDP(n) {
  const dp = [0, 1];
  for (let i = 2; i <= n; i++) {
    dp[i] = dp[i-1] + dp[i-2];
  }
  return dp[n];
}
```
## Follow-up Questions
- When would you use memoization vs tabulation?
- What's the space complexity of bottom-up DP?
- Can every recursive solution be converted to DP?

